<===> README.md
# Detection of var() in color functions

Like dart-sass, an unquoted string is a `var()` if it starts with `var(`,
case-insensitive, and is at least as long as `var(--_)`.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> minimum_length/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: rgb(string.unquote("var(--_)"))}
<===> minimum_length/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(var(--_));
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> mixed_case/rgb/input.scss
a {b: rgb(Var(--x), 2, 3)}
<===> mixed_case/rgb/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(Var(--x), 2, 3);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> uppercase/color/input.scss
a {b: color(VAR(--x))}
<===> uppercase/color/output.css
a {
  b: color(VAR(--x));
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> uppercase/color_space/input.scss
a {b: color(VAR(--s) 1 2 3)}
<===> uppercase/color_space/output.css
a {
  b: color(VAR(--s) 1 2 3);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> uppercase/hsla/input.scss
a {b: hsla(VAR(--c), 0.5)}
<===> uppercase/hsla/output.css
a {
  b: hsla(VAR(--c), 0.5);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> uppercase/rgb/input.scss
a {b: rgb(VAR(--x))}
<===> uppercase/rgb/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(VAR(--x));
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> uppercase/rgba/input.scss
a {b: rgba(VAR(--c), 0.5)}
<===> uppercase/rgba/output.css
a {
  b: rgba(VAR(--c), 0.5);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/too_short/color/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: color(string.unquote("var(x)"))}
<===> error/too_short/color/error
Error: $description: Unknown color space "var(x)".
  ,
2 | a {b: color(string.unquote("var(x)"))}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
<===> error/too_short/color/error-libsass
Error: $description: Unknown color space "var(x)".
  ,
2 | a {b: color(string.unquote("var(x)"))}
  |                            ^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:28  color()
  ,
2 | a {b: color(string.unquote("var(x)"))}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7   root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> error/too_short/rgba/input.scss
@use "sass:string";
a {b: rgba(string.unquote("var(c)"), 0.5)}
<===> error/too_short/rgba/error
Error: $color: var(c) is not a color.
  ,
2 | a {b: rgba(string.unquote("var(c)"), 0.5)}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
<===> error/too_short/rgba/error-libsass
Error: $color: var(c) is not a color.
  ,
2 | a {b: rgba(string.unquote("var(c)"), 0.5)}
  |                           ^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:27  rgba()
  ,
2 | a {b: rgba(string.unquote("var(c)"), 0.5)}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7   root stylesheet
